{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChSPM3fGuepAkfaJtBNDC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't edit files in this session (I only have read and search tools), so here's the change for you to apply. One correction first: GitLab doesn't do caching as a separate stage. You add a `cache:` setting to the jobs that install dependencies. A separate stage wouldn't help anyway, because each job starts on a fresh runner.\n\nProposed `.gitlab-ci.yml`:\n\n```yaml\nstages:\n  - build\n  - test\n\ndefault:\n  cache:\n    key:\n      files:\n        - package-lock.json\n    paths:\n      - .npm/\n    policy: pull-push\n\nbuild:\n  stage: build\n  script:\n    - npm ci --cache .npm --prefer-offline\n    - npm run build\n```\n\n**What this does:**\n- **Caches npm's download cache (`.npm/`), not `node_modules/`.** `npm ci` deletes `node_modules` every time it runs, so caching that folder would do nothing. Keeping the cache inside the project folder is required because GitLab only caches paths inside the project.\n- **`--prefer-offline`** makes npm use the cached packages before going to the registry.\n- **`key: files: [package-lock.json]`** creates a new cache whenever the lockfile changes and reuses it otherwise.\n- **Putting it under `default:`** means any jobs you add to the `test` stage get the same cache. Give those jobs `cache: { policy: pull }` (along with the same `key` and `paths`) so they only read the cache and don't upload it again.\n\n**Two things I noticed in the repo:**\n1. **There's no `package-lock.json` here,** and `npm ci` fails without one. Either the lockfile is somewhere else (if so, set `cache:key:files` to that path) or it needs to be committed.\n2. **The `test` stage has no jobs.** If tests should run on the build output, pass `dist/` (or wherever the build writes) from `build` to the test jobs with `artifacts:`. The cache is meant for dependencies, and GitLab doesn't guarantee it will be there.\n\nIf your runners don't share cache storage (e.g. no S3/GCS cache set up for autoscaled runners), jobs on different machines will miss the cache. In that case, set up a distributed cache on the runners."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_read_input_tokens":13538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":261},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2b48faf-bcc3-413a-bf24-f077ad819a60","uuid":"329c126b-a910-461a-88a5-318eca6f7e4e","timestamp":"2026-11-26T23:12:22.687Z","request_id":"req_011ChSPM3Xb6grYrZN7UE48x"}
